And the types for those are as you expect.

01:05.000 --> 01:10.000
We used helper functions on the Reppel to help us diagnose and solve problems.

01:11.000 --> 01:16.000
So type will let us know the type of a variable or a value.

01:17.000 --> 01:24.000
We can also use DUR to figure out what methods are available for that particular type.

01:25.000 --> 01:39.000
And we can use help to either look at the help for that type or help is more useful when you pass in the specific method that you would like to know more about.

01:40.000 --> 01:43.000
So for example, stir dot is upper.

01:44.000 --> 01:54.000
We'll tell me that this will return true if the string is uppercase and false otherwise, and help will also give us some hints as to what that method expects.

01:56.000 --> 02:15.000
Now strings in Python are delineated either with single quotes or double quotes, but remember that the type of the quote has to match or that is a syntax error.

