04:03.000 --> 04:05.000
In Python, we also have lists.

04:06.000 --> 04:11.000
Remember, do not name your list list.

04:12.000 --> 04:15.000
You'll have a bad time.

04:16.000 --> 04:22.000
As we saw earlier, when I had a bad time, when I named a variable list and completely forgot about it.

04:22.000 --> 04:26.000
And then got weird syntax errors and had to think about it.

04:27.000 --> 04:30.000
So if we have a list called my list.

04:43.000 --> 04:47.000
I can check it out in the REPL. I can ask for its length.

04:47.000 --> 04:54.000
And I can append values to it.

05:01.000 --> 05:06.000
So append because I'm calling it on this list itself.

05:07.000 --> 05:10.000
And the list is mutable meaning the list can be changed.

05:11.000 --> 05:14.000
This is going to go ahead and change my list in place.

05:15.000 --> 05:18.000
I can get values by index.

05:19.000 --> 05:21.000
Remember, list have a zero index.

05:24.000 --> 05:27.000
And that will go ahead and grab the individual items.

05:28.000 --> 05:32.000
I can change items in a list with assignment.

05:33.000 --> 05:35.000
So if I take a look at my list here.

05:36.000 --> 05:42.000
If I wanted to change the zero earth value to get the zero earth value, I would just call that to change it.

05:42.000 --> 05:47.000
I would make an assignment to it.

05:48.000 --> 05:51.000
And now I've modified my list.

05:52.000 --> 05:57.000
If we want to delete elements from a list, we could use the delete keyword.

05:58.000 --> 06:02.000
I would recommend not doing that. It's kind of confusing.

06:03.000 --> 06:08.000
So instead, I would advise you to call pop.

06:09.000 --> 06:12.000
And you can call pop with an index as well.

06:15.000 --> 06:22.000
So pop with no arguments will just pop that last item off the list.

06:23.000 --> 06:27.000
If I wanted to save it at this point, I could assign it to a variable.

06:28.000 --> 06:32.000
And this operation has, in fact, changed my list.

06:32.000 --> 06:35.000
I can also sort my list in two ways.

06:36.000 --> 06:40.000
The first is with the sorted keyword.

06:41.000 --> 06:45.000
The sorted keyword does not change the value of the list.

06:46.000 --> 06:53.000
But if I call my list dot sort because I'm taking that action on a list, which is a mutable type.

06:54.000 --> 06:58.000
That's going to go ahead and modify the values inside.

